## 6. Compatibility with the Classical Criterion

This theorem is **fully compatible** with the **Beale–Kato–Majda (BKM)
criterion**:

$$
\int_0^{T^*} \|\boldsymbol{\omega}\|_{L^\infty}\,d\tau = +\infty
\;\Longleftrightarrow\;
\text{finite-time singularity}.
$$

Bu Theory supplies its **topological mechanism**: the divergence of the BKM
integral corresponds to a **He-Void transition (controlled)**, rather than the
pointwise runaway blow-up classically feared.

